    <h2>Current campaigns</h2>

    <h3>Dom &amp; Davion's Law</h3>
    <p>
      Strengthening protections for children in custody and welfare
      situations where documented warning signs were not acted on. We support
      this legislation alongside the families who carry its names.
    </p>

    <h3>Hailey's Law</h3>
    <p>
      Improving how missing person reports are taken, entered, and tracked by
      law enforcement — so no report sits unentered while hours that matter
      slip away.
    </p>

    <h3>Death investigation standards</h3>
    <p>
      Advocating for stronger training, documentation, and review standards
      when deaths are ruled accidental, undetermined, or suicide despite
      unresolved questions — the gap that
      <a href="/programs/homicides">hidden homicides</a> fall through.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sign the active petitions.</strong> Current petition links are shared from our <a href="/blog">blog</a> and social channels — external petition sites change, so we keep live links there.</li>
      <li><strong>Contact your legislators.</strong> Find your Indiana representatives at <a href="https://iga.in.gov/" rel="noopener">iga.in.gov</a>. A short, personal message about why victims' legislation matters to you outweighs a hundred form letters.</li>
      <li><strong>Show up.</strong> When bills get hearings, presence matters. Watch <a href="/get-involved/events">events</a> for Statehouse days.</li>
      <li><strong>Tell your story.</strong> If your family's experience speaks to one of these gaps and you're willing to share it with lawmakers, <a href="/about/contact">contact us</a> — we'll prepare you and stand with you.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
